.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:annotation		ORCA, PBE0-D3BJ/def2-SVP with CPCM(water), optimisation and analytic frequencies with IR and Raman. This calculation shows that the carboxylate anion has two coupled CO2 stretches instead of one C=O stretch: the out-of-phase (antisymmetric) stretch at 1744.15 cm-1 (unscaled; IR 760.75 km/mol, Raman activity 4.436) and the in-phase stretch, mixed with CH3 deformation, at 1452.48 cm-1 (IR 307.36 km/mol, Raman activity 5.169). No band lies near the 1870-1910 cm-1 of the neutral carbonyl compounds.
.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:application		ORCA
